In article <31588@mimsy.umd.edu> leonard@mimsy.umd.edu (Leonard Dickens ) writes:
>What alignment do you favor?  It seems to me that the best alignment to be
>is Lawful, for the following reasons:
>1) Two of the best artifacts (Mjollnir, Excaliber) available from god. 
>2) Can convert any altar to Lawful, which is good because:
>3) Lawful altars make holy water, i.e., blessings.
>
>Any dissention on this point?  Chaotic characters *do* have a good chance of
>getting Stormbringer from their god.  But unholy water is so... useless.

   Being lawful does have its advantages, but:

1)  You can't pray in hell
2)  There are too many junk artifacts; it usually takes too long to get Mjollnir
    -- do you really need Trollsbane or Sting?
3)  Unholy water have its uses; I always keep a few around
      to keep my gluttonous pets off the food/sacraments and 
      to make cursed scrolls of genocide(have never won a game without these).
4) Gremlins are nonpeaceful to lawful characters( and
    not to mention some other nasties in Hell.)
5) Rustproofed Excalibur can be obtained from fountains.
   With this weapon and some cautious playing you don't really need
any other artifacts.  

>Given that Lawful is the best alignment to have, I always try to convert to 
>Lawfulness as soon as I have a lawful altar and enough monsters in range to
>sacrifice to get over the lawful god's initial displeasure.
>
